{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1551534-is-across-the-eight-directions-useful-for-essence-games","id":1551534,"title":"Is \"Across the Eight Directions\" Useful for Essence Games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-09T02:07:39-07:00","id":1551534,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Is \"Across the Eight Directions\" Useful for Essence Games?","content":"Onyx Path is currently holding a sale, which means that <i>Across the Eight Directions</i> (and some other supplements) is 50% off at DriveThruRPG. This is a supplement for Exalted 3e, but how useful is it if I'm running a game of Essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28792-beron-the-grey","name":"Beron the Grey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28792_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T07:33:11-07:00","id":1551536,"title":"","content":"Pretty good. Its 98% setting material, so it doesn't matter much which version of the game you're playing.<br /> Its also one of the best setting books I've ever read, so feel free to take that as an endorsement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T15:49:50-07:00","id":1551546,"title":"","content":"I've used it for my Exigents quest in order to fill out potential locations, so I'd say it's one of the best 3e books you can grab. Also helps if you need ideas for NPCs for the players to interact with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T16:09:46-07:00","id":1551548,"title":"","content":"As others have said its mostly locations of interest and npcs who inhabit it with plot hooks. The Realm might also be of use since its mostly lore and details about the Scarlet Dynasty, but if you have to pick one 8 Directions has the best scope and would be the more useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-10T12:44:08-07:00","id":1551568,"title":"","content":"It along with <i>The Realm</i> are probably the two most useful for Essence books for the mainline game, IMHO. They are great compliments to one-another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantAr